WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.310
John: Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday, May
5th, 2015, your 35th birthday!

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.460
It's just ridiculously beautiful here—Haaank!

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.860
Oh look, it's Hank!

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.630
Hank is of course using this occasion to Snapchat.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:11.630
John: Don't rock.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:12.630
Hank: Yeah!

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.630
John: It's going to ruin the shot.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.630
Hank: Whee!

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:15.630
John: Oh, it's going to make people sick to
their stomachs.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.630
Hank: Whee!

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.689
John: When your birthday falls on a Tuesday,
it is a great present to me, because it means

00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:20.470
I don't have to make an extra Vlogbrothers
video.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.470
Thank you.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.169
Hank: Well, if you could work out that for
me on…August 27th…

00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:27.240
John: Oh my God you've hurt my feelings!

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.810
Let's move on, it's twenty—August twenty—

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.810
Hank: 23rd?

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.260
John: I don't even wanna be your friend anymore,
let alone your sibling.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.920
I have not gotten you a formal present.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:37.990
Instead, I want to tell you that I will get
you anything you want.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.830
Hank: I want a whole mountain.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.580
John: I cannot buy you a mountain.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.580
I don't have the resources.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.580
Hank: What about a project?

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.650
John: Depends on the project.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.320
I don't wanna do a project that I don't wanna
do.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.710
Hank: What a surprise.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.710
John: But it is your birthday.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.120
Hank: John Green: doesn't wanna do things
he doesn't wanna do.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.110
John: I have a longstanding opposition to
doing things that I don't wanna do.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.100
Hank: I've wanted to do a podcast with you.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.100
John: Oh!

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.100
I like podcasts.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.100
What should it be about?

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.100
Hank: Stuff that we care about.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.100
Stuff that we like.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.100
John: Mm, that's going to bore people.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.939
I really like high-concept podcasts like Night
Vale, or the DeGeorges have that podcast that's

00:01:05.939 --> 00:01:07.759
from the perspective of a cephalopod.

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:08.990
Hank: It's a giant squid, yeah.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:09.990
John: Yeah.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:10.990
Hank: Do you want to ask?

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:11.990
John: Oh!

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:12.990
Oh, yeah.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:13.990
What should we make a podcast about?

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.219
By the way, I don't know why we're not making
our video with that in the background.

00:01:16.219 --> 00:01:17.390
Hank: I mean, I could explain it.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.390
It has to do with—

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.390
John: It has to do with lighting.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.390
Hank: The lighting.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.909
John: So as Hank's birthday present, I am
going to get him a podcast, uh, that we make.

00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:23.909
Hank: Starring us.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:25.899
John: It's starring us, but you guys tell
us what it should be about.

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:29.950
Hank: I like the idea of…I just had this
one.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:30.950
John: Okay.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.270
Hank: What if, uh, every episode we just talk
about a different person, but we pick a name,

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.350
and we just talk about a person with that
name in history.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:41.680
John: Oh, so like the, oh, so it's like "The
Steve Podcast with John and Hank Green."

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.680
Hank: Yeah.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.680
John: Or like "The Sydney Podcast."

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.680
Like, something gender-neutral.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.409
Hank: But it should be two names so that people
are extra confused.

00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:47.409
John: Oh, like, the, uh—

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:50.719
Hank: Like "The Sydney and Jesse Podcast—"

00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:51.840
John: "With John and Hank Green."

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:52.840
Hank: "With John and Hank Green."

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.080
John: And we just talk about Sydneys and Jesses.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.819
But there should be another, there should
be another thing.

00:01:56.819 --> 00:01:59.380
Hank: There's, yeah yeah, segments where we
talk about other stuff we're into, and also

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.659
what's going on in our lives or things.

00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:02.619
John: I'll do like "This Week in AFC Wimbledon."

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:03.721
Like, what's going on in fourth-tier football.

00:02:03.721 --> 00:02:05.390
Hank: Right, because everybody's so interested
in that.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.390
John: Everyone is.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.530
Well what is something that you care about?

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.489
Hank: I could do Mars, 'cause I've cared about
that forever.

00:02:09.489 --> 00:02:10.789
John: "This week in Mars and AFC Wimbledon!"

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:11.789
The—

00:02:11.789 --> 00:02:14.379
Hank: And Mars is so much more interesting
than AFC Wimbledon, so everyone will listen

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:18.900
for Mars, we have to do AFC Wimbledon first,
so people have to sit through it to get to

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:19.900
the Mars news.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.230
John: Strongly disagree.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:27.520
Mars is a planet that humans can't inhabit;
AFC Wimbledon is a club made out of humans.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.210
And aren't humans the most interesting thing
in the world, really?

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.890
Hank: He says as he points the camera just
at himself.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:34.680
John: Whose birthday is it anyway?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.540
It's my birthday, right?

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.150
Isn't it August 27th or 22nd?

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.430
No one can remember.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.200
I'm not sure it's sustainable, are there enough
Sydneys and Jesses?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.200
Hank: Oh, sure.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.200
John: Name two Sydneys.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.200
'Cause—"

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.049
Hank: My mom, Sydney Green.

00:02:47.049 --> 00:02:48.290
Sydney, Australia?

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:49.540
John: Ah.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.879
Is there a Jesse, Australia?

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:53.780
If you like this idea, let us know some Sydneys
and Jesses in comments.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:55.720
Oh no, it, it's leaving me.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:56.730
Was that your Blue Steel?

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.910
On three, uh, our best Blue Steel.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.060
One, Two, Three.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.719
So we need you to tell us what our podcast
is going to be about, if it's going to be

00:03:03.719 --> 00:03:06.930
about Sydneys and Jesses, some Sydneys and
Jesses we can talk about, who has the best

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.550
Blue Steel, and if AFC Wimbledon or Mars is
more important.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.550
Hank: Right.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.280
John: Would the earth be different if there
were no Mars?

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.159
Hank: I mean, yes?

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:15.159
John: How?

00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:16.159
Hank: We, well—

00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:20.140
John: The sky would look different at night,
but if there were no AFC Wimbledon, the core

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:22.010
of human history would change.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.049
Hank: [Burps] So also for my birthday.

00:03:24.049 --> 00:03:25.049
John: Yeah?

00:03:25.049 --> 00:03:26.290
Hank: I have to make a video this week.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.290
John: Yes.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:31.129
Hank: I would make, like to make that video
a, a kind of, uh, Vlogbrothers Olympics.

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:32.129
John: I may do it.

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:33.280
Hank: Where you and I compete in, in events.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.640
John: How many events?

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:35.640
Hank: Twenty.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.640
John: No!

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.110
Hank: It's going to be a dodecacathlon.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.110
John: No!

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.050
What about like a, no, like a septathlon,
or maybe a quadragocon.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:44.879
Hank: Okay, "quadragocon" I will go for.

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:46.360
John: So we're doing a four event quadragocon.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.960
Hank: No no no, fourteen.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.400
Quadragocon is fourteen.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.400
Obviously.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.629
The first event is who wins that Blue Steel.

00:03:52.629 --> 00:03:53.629
John: Okay.

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:54.629
Hank: Okay.

00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:55.629
John: Hank, Happy Birthday.

00:03:55.629 --> 00:03:59.010
I will, uh, see you, I will continue to see
you after I turn off the camera.

